# The digests the browser compile asks of Node's `crypto`, answered from the Term definitions every backend's native
# digest is held equal to (native/shared/cryptography: sha256.tree, md5.tree). The compiler's ports are emitted for
# node, so they call `createHash` from `node:crypto`. The bundle aliases `crypto` and `node:crypto` to browser/crypto.ts,
# which is Node's shape over these tasks: each `update` becomes bytes here, and `digest` answers the lowercase hex.

load @term/base/native/shared/cryptography/sha256
  find calculate-sha256
  find encode-utf-8

load @term/base/native/shared/cryptography/md5
  find calculate-md5

# the UTF-8 bytes of a text, as node's `update` reads a string with no encoding (a lone surrogate as U+FFFD)
task text-bytes
  take value, like text
  like list
    like number
  send back
    call encode-utf-8
      read value

# SHA-256 of a byte list, as 64 lowercase hex characters
task sha256-hex
  take input
    like list
      like number
  like text
  send back
    call calculate-sha256
      read input

# MD5 of a byte list, as 32 lowercase hex characters
task md5-hex
  take input
    like list
      like number
  like text
  send back
    call calculate-md5
      read input
